 "observations": [
  "t3code's ClaudeAdapterV2 only consumes stream_event thinking deltas; assistant text is taken from the per-block `assistant` snapshot. So the 52 KB answer is NOT rendered incrementally: during the 18 s stream the UI shows 'Working for Ns' + the reasoning line, and the whole markdown renders at once when the text block completes (verified by a mid-stream screenshot). The render spike (renderer ~170% of a core, total ~190%, +~90 MB RSS) therefore falls at the start of the settled phase.",
  "steady ~10-14% total CPU during streaming comes mostly from renderer+GPU (Working-timer repaint under software GL); server CPU ~0-2% between frames.",
  "about 8 s after the turn another short server+renderer CPU burst (~100%) occurs (post-turn work such as checkpointing)."
 ],
 "caveats": [
  "software rendering (Mesa llvmpipe via ANGLE/GLX) under Xvfb inflates GPU-process CPU vs. a real GPU",
  "running as root with --no-sandbox; unpackaged electron run (not the AppImage, not asar)",
  "single run per phase; 500 ms sampling misses sub-sample spikes and CPU of processes that live < 500 ms",
  "RSS double counts shared pages across Chromium processes (zygote/renderer/gpu); PSS sum is the better total",
  "fake provider CLI, no network/API latency; real Claude Code CLI process (~hundreds of MB node/bun) is NOT included - fake is a ~10 MB python process"
 ],
